{"name":"Juniper","hex":"#74918e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Juniper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from English.","A unisex given name from English.\nA female given name from English.\nA male given name from English."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Juniper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Juniper","blocks":[{"text":"Junipers are coniferous trees and shrubs in the genus Juniperus of the cypress family Cupressaceae. Depending on the taxonomic authority, between 50 and 67 species of junipers are widely distributed throughout the Northern Hemisphere as far south as tropical Africa, as far north as the Arctic, and parts of Asia and Central America. The highest-known juniper forest occurs at an altitude of 4,900 metres (16,100 ft) in southeastern Tibet and the northern Himalayas, creating one of the highest tree lines on earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Juniperus_osteosperma_1.jpg/330px-Juniperus_osteosperma_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juniper","wikidata":"Q25662"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Juniperus_communis_cones.jpg/500px-Juniperus_communis_cones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Juniperus_communis_cones.jpg/500px-Juniperus_communis_cones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cones and leaves of Juniperus communis","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJuniperus_communis_cones.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Jun_chin_close.jpg/500px-Jun_chin_close.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Jun_chin_close.jpg/500px-Jun_chin_clo